IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sscba-types`
IMPORT `sscba-rules`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL
-- GOAL.

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Employee case` HAS
    `a week of earnings`                                IS A MAYBE `Week of earnings`
    `sickness`                                          IS A MAYBE `Sick pay facts`
    `maternity`                                         IS A MAYBE `Maternity facts`

DECLARE `Employee position` HAS
    `primary Class 1 contribution`                      IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `secondary Class 1 contribution`                    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `weekly statutory sick pay`                         IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `statutory sick pay for a day`                      IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `statutory sick pay entitlement limit`              IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `periods of incapacity link`                        IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `entitled to statutory maternity pay`               IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `earliest start of the maternity pay period`        IS A MAYBE DATE
    `maternity pay for the first 6 weeks`               IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `maternity pay for the remaining weeks`             IS A MAYBE NUMBER

@ref ss 8, 9, 152, 155, 157, 164-166, 171
@export default The position of an employee under the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (UK): primary and secondary Class 1 contributions on a week's earnings (ss 8-9); statutory sick pay weekly and daily amounts, the entitlement limit and whether periods of incapacity link (ss 152-157); and statutory maternity pay entitlement, the earliest start of the maternity pay period and the weekly rates (ss 164-166, 0 rates where not entitled). Each is NOTHING where its facts are not given. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS AN `Employee case`  @desc Any week of earnings, sickness facts and maternity facts
GIVETH AN `Employee position`
`the employee position for` c MEANS
    `Employee position` WITH
        `primary Class 1 contribution`                  IS
            CONSIDER c's `a week of earnings`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST w  THEN JUST (`the primary Class 1 contribution on` w)
        `secondary Class 1 contribution`                IS
            CONSIDER c's `a week of earnings`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST w  THEN JUST (`the secondary Class 1 contribution on` w)
        `weekly statutory sick pay`                     IS
            CONSIDER c's `sickness`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST s  THEN JUST (`the weekly rate of statutory sick pay for` s)
        `statutory sick pay for a day`                  IS
            CONSIDER c's `sickness`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST s  THEN JUST (`the statutory sick pay for a day for` s)
        `statutory sick pay entitlement limit`          IS
            CONSIDER c's `sickness`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST s  THEN JUST (`the entitlement limit for` s)
        `periods of incapacity link`                    IS
            CONSIDER c's `sickness`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST s  THEN JUST (`the periods of incapacity link for` s)
        `entitled to statutory maternity pay`           IS
            CONSIDER c's `maternity`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST m  THEN JUST (`is entitled to statutory maternity pay` m)
        `earliest start of the maternity pay period`    IS
            CONSIDER c's `maternity`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST m  THEN JUST (`the earliest start of the maternity pay period for` m)
        `maternity pay for the first 6 weeks`           IS
            CONSIDER c's `maternity`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST m  THEN JUST (IF `is entitled to statutory maternity pay` m THEN `the first 6 weeks' rate for` m ELSE 0)
        `maternity pay for the remaining weeks`         IS
            CONSIDER c's `maternity`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST m  THEN JUST (IF `is entitled to statutory maternity pay` m THEN `the later weeks' rate for` m ELSE 0)
